WEBVTT

00:00.720 --> 00:05.120
In this problem, we're asked
to figure out the length of BC.

00:05.120 --> 00:06.850
We have a bunch
of triangles here,

00:06.850 --> 00:10.030
and some lengths of sides,
and a couple of right angles.

00:10.030 --> 00:12.290
And so maybe we can
establish similarity

00:12.290 --> 00:13.715
between some of the triangles.

00:13.715 --> 00:16.340
There's actually three different
triangles that I can see here.

00:16.340 --> 00:19.372
This triangle, this triangle,
and this larger triangle.

00:19.372 --> 00:21.080
If we can establish
some similarity here,

00:21.080 --> 00:23.070
maybe we can use
ratios between sides

00:23.070 --> 00:26.890
somehow to figure
out what BC is.

00:26.890 --> 00:30.050
So when you look at it, you have
a right angle right over here.

00:30.050 --> 00:33.150
So in triangle BDC, you
have one right angle.

00:33.150 --> 00:36.450
In triangle ABC, you
have another right angle.

00:36.450 --> 00:40.870
If we can show that they have
another corresponding set

00:40.870 --> 00:42.890
of angles are congruent
to each other,

00:42.890 --> 00:44.550
then we can show
that they're similar.

00:44.550 --> 00:49.950
And actually, both of those
triangles, both BDC and ABC,

00:49.950 --> 00:51.879
both share this angle
right over here.

00:51.879 --> 00:53.920
So if they share that
angle, then they definitely

00:53.920 --> 00:55.400
share two angles.

00:55.400 --> 00:57.550
So they both share that
angle right over there.

00:57.550 --> 00:59.100
Let me do that in
a different color

00:59.100 --> 01:02.410
just to make it different
than those right angles.

01:02.410 --> 01:04.370
They both share
that angle there.

01:04.370 --> 01:06.680
And so we know that
two triangles that

01:06.680 --> 01:11.710
have at least two
congruent angles,

01:11.710 --> 01:14.750
they're going to be
similar triangles.

01:14.750 --> 01:22.370
So we know that
triangle ABC-- We

01:22.370 --> 01:25.760
went from the unlabeled angle,
to the yellow right angle,

01:25.760 --> 01:27.274
to the orange angle.

01:27.274 --> 01:28.440
So let me write it this way.

01:37.600 --> 01:38.800
ABC.

01:38.800 --> 01:40.510
And we want to do
this very carefully

01:40.510 --> 01:43.550
here because the same
points, or the same vertices,

01:43.550 --> 01:46.052
might not play the same
role in both triangles.

01:46.052 --> 01:48.510
So we want to make sure we're
getting the similarity right.

01:48.510 --> 01:53.080
White vertex to the
90 degree angle vertex

01:53.080 --> 01:55.160
to the orange vertex.

01:55.160 --> 01:59.840
That is going to be similar
to triangle-- so which

01:59.840 --> 02:02.480
is the one that is neither a
right angle-- so we're looking

02:02.480 --> 02:04.674
at the smaller triangle
right over here.

02:04.674 --> 02:06.590
Which is the one that
is neither a right angle

02:06.590 --> 02:07.600
or the orange angle?

02:07.600 --> 02:09.785
Well it's going to be
vertex B. Vertex B had

02:09.785 --> 02:12.160
the right angle when you think
about the larger triangle.

02:12.160 --> 02:14.300
But we haven't thought
about just that little angle

02:14.300 --> 02:15.500
right over there.

02:15.500 --> 02:17.460
So we start at
vertex B, then we're

02:17.460 --> 02:19.140
going to go to the right angle.

02:19.140 --> 02:24.530
The right angle is
vertex D. And then

02:24.530 --> 02:28.070
we go to vertex C,
which is in orange.

02:28.070 --> 02:31.170
So we have shown that
they are similar.

02:31.170 --> 02:33.820
And now that we know
that they are similar,

02:33.820 --> 02:37.594
we can attempt to take
ratios between the sides.

02:37.594 --> 02:38.760
And so let's think about it.

02:38.760 --> 02:40.520
We know what the
length of AC is.

02:40.520 --> 02:44.320
AC is going to be equal to 8.

02:44.320 --> 02:45.740
6 plus 2.

02:45.740 --> 02:50.680
So we know that AC-- what's
the corresponding side

02:50.680 --> 02:52.340
on this triangle
right over here?

02:52.340 --> 02:54.131
So you could literally
look at the letters.

02:54.131 --> 02:57.800
A and C is going to
correspond to BC.

02:57.800 --> 03:00.310
The first and the third,
first and the third.

03:00.310 --> 03:04.180
AC is going to correspond to BC.

03:04.180 --> 03:06.180
And so this is interesting
because we're already

03:06.180 --> 03:07.660
involving BC.

03:07.660 --> 03:10.490
And so what is it
going to correspond to?

03:10.490 --> 03:16.180
And then if we look at BC
on the larger triangle,

03:16.180 --> 03:20.080
BC is going to correspond to
what on the smaller triangle?

03:20.080 --> 03:22.770
It's going to correspond to DC.

03:22.770 --> 03:24.850
And it's good because
we know what AC, is

03:24.850 --> 03:26.220
and we know it DC is.

03:26.220 --> 03:27.860
And so we can solve for BC.

03:27.860 --> 03:30.410
So I want to take one more
step to show you what we just

03:30.410 --> 03:32.950
did here, because BC is
playing two different roles.

03:32.950 --> 03:34.710
On this first statement
right over here,

03:34.710 --> 03:35.670
we're thinking of BC.

03:38.280 --> 03:41.240
BC on our smaller
triangle corresponds

03:41.240 --> 03:43.790
to AC on our larger triangle.

03:43.790 --> 03:45.560
And then in the
second statement,

03:45.560 --> 03:48.860
BC on our larger
triangle corresponds

03:48.860 --> 03:51.840
to DC on our smaller triangle.

03:51.840 --> 03:53.670
So in both of these cases.

03:53.670 --> 03:56.480
So these are larger
triangles and then

03:56.480 --> 03:59.920
this is from the smaller
triangle right over here.

03:59.920 --> 04:01.640
Corresponding sides.

04:01.640 --> 04:03.510
And this is a cool
problem because BC

04:03.510 --> 04:07.530
plays two different
roles in both triangles.

04:07.530 --> 04:09.690
But now we have enough
information to solve for BC.

04:09.690 --> 04:17.360
We know that AC is equal to 8.

04:17.360 --> 04:18.750
6 plus 2 is 8.

04:18.750 --> 04:20.610
And we know the
DC is equal to 2.

04:20.610 --> 04:21.660
That's given.

04:21.660 --> 04:23.390
And now we can cross multiply.

04:23.390 --> 04:27.360
8 times 2 is 16 is
equal to BC times BC--

04:27.360 --> 04:30.370
is equal to BC squared.

04:30.370 --> 04:33.650
And so BC is going to be equal
to the principal root of 16,

04:33.650 --> 04:34.960
which is 4.

04:34.960 --> 04:39.930
BC is equal to 4.

04:39.930 --> 04:40.610
And we're done.

04:40.610 --> 04:42.340
And the hardest part
about this problem

04:42.340 --> 04:45.200
is just realizing that BC
plays two different roles

04:45.200 --> 04:49.214
and just keeping your
head straight on those two

04:49.214 --> 04:49.880
different roles.

04:49.880 --> 04:51.630
And just to make it
clear, let me actually

04:51.630 --> 04:53.490
draw these two
triangles separately.

04:53.490 --> 04:56.935
So if I drew ABC separately,
it would look like this.

04:59.700 --> 05:02.090
So this is my triangle, ABC.

05:05.370 --> 05:07.680
And then this is a right angle.

05:07.680 --> 05:10.490
This is our orange angle.

05:10.490 --> 05:13.187
We know the length of this
side right over here is 8.

05:13.187 --> 05:15.770
And we know that the length of
this side, which we figured out

05:15.770 --> 05:17.730
through this problem is 4.

05:17.730 --> 05:22.010
Then if we wanted to draw BDC,
we would draw it like this.

05:22.010 --> 05:27.780
So BDC looks like this.

05:27.780 --> 05:31.340
So this is BDC.

05:31.340 --> 05:33.080
That's a little bit
easier to visualize

05:33.080 --> 05:35.660
because we've already--
This is our right angle.

05:35.660 --> 05:37.940
This is our orange angle.

05:37.940 --> 05:42.550
And this is 4, and this
right over here is 2.

05:42.550 --> 05:43.930
And I did it this
way to show you

05:43.930 --> 05:47.660
that you have to flip this
triangle over and rotate it

05:47.660 --> 05:50.294
just to have a
similar orientation.

05:50.294 --> 05:52.460
And then it might make it
look a little bit clearer.

05:52.460 --> 05:54.050
So if you found
this part confusing,

05:54.050 --> 05:57.750
I encourage you to try to flip
and rotate BDC in such a way

05:57.750 --> 06:00.620
that it seems to
look a lot like ABC.

06:00.620 --> 06:02.250
And then this ratio
should hopefully

06:02.250 --> 06:04.620
make a lot more sense.
